        "bosses": {
          "fumaca": {
            "nome": "Coal",
            "fala": "You quick? I'm smoke, kid. Blink and I'm gone — and you eat it in the dark."
          },
          "turco": {
            "nome": "The Collector",
            "fala": "All of Marelia owes me. Now {suaGangue} does too. Round here, whoever can't pay in cash pays in bone."
          },
          "espeto": {
            "nome": "Gut-Stabber",
            "fala": "The Lowside's been mine since the Shadow hit the ditch. Took my spots? Fine. Come take the rest."
          },
          "sala": {
            "nome": "Rust",
            "fala": "Climbed ten floors just to get dropped on the last one? Respect the effort. Changes nothing."
          },
          "zefa": {
            "nome": "The Beast",
            "fala": "I raised half the kids {suaGangue} beat to get up here. Sit down. Your punishment's gonna take a while."
          },
          "doutor": {
            "nome": "The Accountant",
            "fala": "Do the math, kid. You've got two fighters. I've got the whole Hilltop owing me favors. Now go home."
          },
          "costura": {
            "nome": "The Patchwork",
            "fala": "All of Marelia was mine once. Six blocks in hand, the Rooftop under my feet. But this thing won't stitch — not even I held it. Come up here and I'll show you the hard way."
          }
        },
        "territorios": {
          "pista": {
            "nome": "The Track",
            "desc": "The asphalt down below. Kids darting the light, snatching chains, selling gum. Nobody important — but everyone starts here. Alan did too."
          },
          "feira": {
            "nome": "The Market",
            "desc": "The stalls, the vendors, the spliced power lines. No shooting here — just debt. The Collector writes it all down, and the Collector collects it all."
          },
          "baixada": {
            "nome": "The Lowside",
            "desc": "Across the train tracks. The Shadow's crew split three ways when he died. Crimson, Cold and the Leftovers bite each other before they bite you."
          },
          "vila": {
            "nome": "The Projects",
            "desc": "The blocks, the ten-floor towers, the unlit stairwell. The crew runs it bottom to top. To reach the owner you climb it all taking hits."
          },
          "morro": {
            "nome": "The Hill",
            "desc": "The hillside slum, the concrete stairway that changes shape with every new rooftop. The spots, the firework boys. Nobody comes down the Hill the same."
          },
          "alto": {
            "nome": "The Hilltop",
            "desc": "Past the steel door. The Five nearly became a council — pulled half the Hill into one hand before the Patchwork came, and before you."
          },
          "laje": {
            "nome": "The Rooftop",
            "desc": "The top. On one side, all of Marelia watching. On the other, the Patchwork — the only one who ever held six blocks at once. This is where you find out if seven can be held."
          }
        },
        "falas": {
          "ponto": "{territorio}. This spot belongs to {gangue}, pal. {suaGangue} doesn't walk through here for free."
        },
        "abertura": [
          "Sit down, I'll tell you how this works.",
          "Marelia has no king. A gang in every alley, each one thinking it rules the world 'cause it rules one street.",
          "Want to rise? Start on the Track, down below. Take the small gangs' spots, then face the region's heavy — the one holding the flag.",
          "Take the block, the next one opens. Block by block up to the Rooftop.",
          "Up top there's someone nobody knows the real name of. They just call him the Patchwork. He once pulled six blocks under one flag. Nobody ever came closer to owning Marelia.",
          "You'll have to go through him. Good luck, kid — you'll need it."
        ],
        "final": {
          "code": "THE CLIMB ENDS HERE",
          "titulo": "MARELIA WON'T STITCH",
          "paragrafos": [
            "{gangue} put the Patchwork down on the Rooftop. All of Marelia saw it.",
            "And then you understood what he already knew. Two weeks and the map was split again — blocks pulling one way, spots pulling another. Nobody holds this city. He didn't. You didn't.",
            "Years later a kid with weird hair would do what neither of you could. His name was Alan. But that's another story — and you're in it, right at the start."
          ]
        }
